  "text": "Thank you all for flagging these issues. Let me summarize what I'm hearing before I make a decision. Jonas, your cash-flow model shows the project doesn't pass our hurdle at $6 million — the approvable purchase price is $4.8 million. Elena, the 30% investment tax credit is available only if we own the equipment, which the current purchase structure allows. Victor, we can only deploy $2 million in cash without breaching our liquidity floor, and the remaining $2.8 million would need a five-year term loan. Rina, there's an additional $400,000 performance bond requirement and a commissioning certificate gate before energization. So the total upfront commitment is effectively $6.4 million, not $6 million, and the project doesn't clear our hurdle even at $6 million. Before I settle, I want to consider whether we can renegotiate the purchase price down to a level that makes economic sense given all these factors. Let me think through the numbers and then record my decision."
}
